Fix a broken `ExtensionUrlTemplate(...)` call inside the haybarn
engine's `#ifdef WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS` branch of
`extension_load.cpp`. The branch references `&config` (out of scope:
function signature is `TryInitialLoad(DatabaseInstance &db, ...)`) and
passes only 2 of the 3 required arguments.

Engine's actual signature:

    static string ExtensionUrlTemplate(
        optional_ptr<const DatabaseInstance> db,
        const ExtensionRepository &repository,
        const string &version);

The bug only manifests when the engine is compiled with
`WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS=1` (this repo's *_loadable build matrix
entries). Native builds and non-loadable wasm builds preprocessor-skip
the branch.

If/when the engine fork merges this fix upstream, the patch becomes a
"previously applied" no-op and can be deleted.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@
 		direct_load = false;
 		string extension_name = ApplyExtensionAlias(extension);
 #ifdef WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS
-		string url_template = ExtensionUrlTemplate(&config, "");
+		string url_template = ExtensionUrlTemplate(&db, ExtensionRepository{}, "");
 		string url = ExtensionFinalizeUrlTemplate(url_template, extension_name);

 		char *str = (char *)EM_ASM_PTR(
